From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] proxied GL extension functions resolve through the host's eglGetProcAddress; a still missing host function answers 0 (named in the log) instead of aborting the process

proxy_library_builder.cc takes the host function of a known proxied name from dlsym of the host library and, when that fails, gave it the thunk DoBadThunk, which was
LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL. Mesa's libGLESv2.so exports only core GL: its EXT/OES/KHR/ANGLE extension functions (485 names of the guest libGLESv2 proxy) are reachable only through
eglGetProcAddress. Gecko's GL loader tries eglGetProcAddress and then dlsym of the library, so it got a non-NULL pointer for such a name and calling it aborted
Fennec's GPU process ("Bad thunk call before ..." in its component log). The parent's main thread then waited for ever for that process's sync IPC reply (MOZ_LOG ipc:
"Send seqno=-29, xid=-29", never answered): no page request, no beacon. Now a GL library's missing function is looked up with the host libEGL's eglGetProcAddress
(HostGlFunction); what the driver lacks too gets a thunk of its own (x86_64 host: a 22-byte stub per name) that logs the name and returns 0, as a driver without the
function gives a caller that ignores a missing extension. Regression: tests/apps/hello-arm64 (missingGlFunctions). Module libberberis_arm64.

